# Light integrity header #light-integrity

This document carries a lightweight integrity digest directly in front matter.
It is not a legal or identity signature, but it lets validators detect content
changes against the canonical AST.

Run the CLI after editing:

```sh
nodx integrity examples/playground/16-light-integrity.nodx
```

Then replace `integrity.value` with the printed `sha256-...` value. The
validator recomputes the digest with the `integrity` field excluded, so any
later content change invalidates the header value until the document is
re-signed.

:::note
Use the future package Signature profile for authorship, keys, trust policy,
and signed assets. This front matter field is intentionally light.
:::
